There's a pattern in those deaths in Nethack; I've encountered some of
the following...

a foocubus removing your gloves while wielding a cockatrice,
an electric eel disintegrating your ring of levitation while above the sea,
a spellcaster destroying your boots levitation above sea or your gloves
while wielding a cockatrice corpse while not having MR,
a monster attacking with fire while you're using an icy path across water,
a nymph stealing your blindfold while at the door of Medusa's chamber,
a covetous monster stealing your single MR resource and applying the touch
of death,

The "Correct Way"[tm] (some call it the paranoic way) to pass water in
Nethack is the following; fill the water with boulders AND get levitating
AND wear water walking AND put on an amulet of magical breathing AND ride
a flying steed. This gives you a 99% of survival chance. Omitting any of
the above will reduce your chance significantly. Anyway; the RNG will find
a way to trigger the remaining 1%.

